WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.491 --> 00:00:01.910
- [Eddie] I think it's
really important to show

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:04.189
your true and authentic face to the world.

00:00:04.189 --> 00:00:05.600
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.890
If you don't know who you are and

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.380
you're not presenting that to the world,

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.446
how are other people
gonna know who you are?

00:00:11.446 --> 00:00:12.654
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.654 --> 00:00:14.760
- I'm Eddie Jarel Jonesx
with an X on the end

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.590
and I am a member of the
Legendary House of Garcon

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.203
and I walk Butch Queen in Drags Runway.

00:00:20.203 --> 00:00:21.036
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.036 --> 00:00:23.006
- I walk, I eat, I slay,
I walk, I eat, I slay.

00:00:23.006 --> 00:00:28.006
Judges, your score! Tens across the board!

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.900
- [Eddie] Makeup led me to being able to

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.220
explore my gender on my own terms.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.140
Being non-binary is
literally going against

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.250
the gender construct that society has set.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.980
For me, gender is like a shower nozzle,

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.810
where it's like you
have hot, you have cold,

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.270
and then you have everything in-between.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.980
Nobody is all hot, nobody is all cold,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.360
it's just what you've been allowed to

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.740
explore in your day-to-day life.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.560
Makeup is like my armor.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.670
For my daytime face, I don't
do like a triple-stacked lash.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:00.630
That's for the Ball, that's for nighttime.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.700
Makeup has always been
a tool in my community

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.900
for people to be the person they are or

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.690
who they really want to be and I think

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:09.710
that's the best way to sum up a Ball.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.800
I can be this person in this Ballroom and

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.570
this is setting me up to be this person

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.250
out in the real world.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.080
As open as the Ballroom community is,

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.025
many may think that gender roles are like

00:01:19.025 --> 00:01:22.260
no big deal, which is
completely incorrect!

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.100
Every category has female
figure and male figure,

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.090
but that's not necessarily how I identify.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:30.890
I've seen categories
like Androgynous Face,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.090
that's a huge step towards breaking those

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.300
gender roles and I think it's really going

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.130
to be ground shaking.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.760
I think in today's
world, there are way more

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.361
representations of all types of people

00:01:42.361 --> 00:01:45.370
expressing themselves through
hair, beauty, and makeup.

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.908
And it just really helps children to see

00:01:47.908 --> 00:01:50.090
there is someone else out there like you

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.620
and they're doing it.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.169
That's really what my work is here to do.

00:01:54.169 --> 00:01:55.400
(upbeat music)

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.950
- All right ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.930
this is the final battle!

